Z||000007||loafer87gt||10-17-2001||11:56 PM||||One of the girls I used to be in Air Cadets with is now an F-18 pilot in the Canadian Airforce. On a related note, our big paper plant (Weyerhauser) in Saskatchewan was shut down today as somebody sent envelopes containing some powder substance to employees. No doubt a prank, but a very unfunny one. I hope the company will track the guy down and send him looking for a new job. The company says it lost over $2 million in productivity because of the false scare. The real scary thing is because of our wonderful Prime Minister's spending cutbacks our Biohazard team for all of Canada is made up of 27 individuals. Yep, that works out to about two per province. Needless to say if an act of Bioterror ever occured, we would be SOL.||||reg||1
